Trimmed (not present here)
  - CMakeLists.txt, cmake/, README.md, and the submodules' build systems,
    docs, tests and CI files: build.rs compiles the sources directly.
  - src/PlatformCrypto.c: crates/stream/src/crypto.rs implements the same
    Plt* functions in Rust, so no OpenSSL or mbedTLS is linked.
  - src/ConnectionTester.c (LiTestClientConnectivity) and src/SimpleStun.c
    (LiFindExternalAddressIP4): public helpers Latch never calls.
    Limelight.h still declares them; nothing may call them.
  - src/RecorderCallbacks.c: only used when LC_DEBUG_RECORD_MODE is defined.
  - enet/compress.c: ENet's range coder; moonlight never enables compression.
  - nanors rs16*, oblas16*: the 16-bit field code; moonlight uses GF(2^8).
  Everything else is byte-for-byte upstream except the two patches below.

Local patches
  1. src/ControlStream.c: enet_peer_timeout(peer, 2, 10000, 10000) becomes
     enet_peer_timeout(peer, 3, 15000, 30000). Latch streams often cross
     a Tailscale peer relay on a long path, where a burst of loss silences
     the reliable control channel for seconds; upstream's 10 s limit then
     declared the PC dead and ended long sessions with "Connection lost
     (code -1)". A dead PC is still noticed within 30 s.
  2. src/SdpGenerator.c: the video bitrate latch is capped at 150000 kbps
     instead of GFE's 100000. Sunshine has no 100 Mbps limit and Latch's
     bitrate setting goes to 150 Mbps.

Re-vendoring
  Check out the new upstream commit with submodules, copy src/, enet/*.c,
  enet/include/, enet/LICENSE, nanors/rs.[ch], nanors/deps/obl/{oblas_common,
  oblas_lite}.[ch], nanors/deps/obl/gf2_8_*.h and nanors/LICENSE, drop the
  files listed above, re-apply both patches, update SOURCES in build.rs if
  upstream added or removed files, and update the commits here. Then run
  `cargo test -p latch-stream` and a live stream_real test.
